   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Water\n\nCaustic light ripples across a dark water surface with gentle refraction, drawn in WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene wants a calm, aquatic atmosphere with gentle refracted highlights.\n- You need a cool, dark blue backdrop that moves slowly without pulling focus.\n- The brief calls for depth or flow imagery (data lakes, streaming, calm).\n\nAvoid when:\n- The palette must be warm or vibrant: water reads cool by design; recolor via `color_highlight` and `color_back` or choose another shader.\n- You want sharp geometric motion: use shader-swirl or shader-dot-orbit.\n- Bright caustics would fight small text: lower `caustic` and `highlights` or use a solid backdrop.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- color_back (color): Water color, default \"#16202b\"\n- color_highlight (color): Highlight color, default \"#7a9ab5\"\n- highlights (number, 0-1): Highlights, default 0.3\n- layering (number, 0-1): Layering, default 0.5\n- edges (number, 0-1): Edges, default 0.8\n- waves (number, 0-1): Waves, default 0.3\n- caustic (number, 0-1): Caustic, default 0.1\n- size (number, 0-1): Size, default 1\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 0.8\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
